.TH VMLITE 1 "2026-11-18" "vmlite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vmlite \- reproducible local KVM/libvirt virtual machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vmlite
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICONFIG\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vmlite
creates and manages local KVM/libvirt guests from a JSON configuration file.
State is project-local under
.I .vmlite/
next to the configuration file. Running
.B vmlite
without a command prints help. Passing a configuration path without a command
is an implicit
.BR "vmlite up" .
.PP
The default configuration file is
.IR vm.json .
.PP
The
.BR start ", " stop ", and " restart
commands also accept a managed VM name, resolved from
.IR .vmlite/NAME.json ,
so the configuration file is not required.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B up
Create or start the VM.
.TP
.B init
Write a starter JSON configuration from an embedded example template.
.TP
.B provision
Run pending provisioners, or finish an automated installer.
.TP
.B status
Show VM, installer, IP, and provisioner state.
.TP
.B start
Start a stopped VM. The argument may be a config path or a managed VM name.
.TP
.B stop
Gracefully stop a running VM. The argument may be a config path or a managed VM
name.
.TP
.B restart
Reboot a running VM or start a stopped VM. The argument may be a config path or
a managed VM name.
.TP
.B ssh
Open a shell or run a command in the guest.
.TP
.B scp
Copy a host file into the guest.
.TP
.B console
Attach to the serial console or print graphical details.
.TP
.B list
List managed VMs in the state directory.
.TP
.B destroy
Remove the VM and managed files.
.TP
.B validate
Validate a configuration without changing anything.
.TP
.B schema
Print the JSON Schema for vmlite configurations.
.TP
.B install
Install host dependencies and the vmlite binary.
.TP
.B doctor
Check host readiness without changing anything.
.TP
.B version
Print the vmlite version.
.TP
.B help
Show top-level or command-specific help.
.SH OPTIONS
Flags belong after the command and accept either
.B \-name
or
.BR \-\-name .
Use
.B vmlite help \fICOMMAND\fR
or
.B vmlite \fICOMMAND\fR \-\-help
for command-specific options.
.TP
.B \-\-connect \fIURI\fR
libvirt connection URI. Defaults to
.B qemu:///system
when available.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir \fIDIR\fR
State directory. Defaults to
.I .vmlite
next to the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print actions without changing anything.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is a JSON object. The default file is
.IR vm.json .
.B vmlite init
writes a starter file from one of the embedded examples:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite init
vmlite init --template minimal
vmlite init --template arch-script --name arch-dev
vmlite init --list
.fi
.RE
.PP
A minimal cloud-image configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "name": "dev",
  "memory": 2048,
  "cpus": 2,
  "source": {
    "type": "cloud_image",
    "path": "/var/cache/vmlite/ubuntu-24.04.img"
  },
  "disk": { "size": 10, "format": "qcow2" },
  "network": { "mode": "default" },
  "graphics": { "type": "none" }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set
.B source.type
to
.BR none ,
.BR cloud_image ,
.BR install_tree ,
.BR iso ,
.BR disk ,
or
.BR pxe .
ISO sources can select an unattended installer with
.BR source.installer .
.PP
Validate and run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite validate vm.json
vmlite up vm.json
vmlite status vm.json
vmlite destroy --force vm.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Managed state, disks, keys, and installer media live under
.I .vmlite/
next to the configuration. Downloaded media is cached under
.IR ~/.cache/vmlite/ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I vm.json
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I .vmlite/NAME.json
Managed state for the VM named
.IR NAME .
Power commands can use
.I NAME
directly instead of the configuration path.
.TP
.I .vmlite/
Project-local state, disks, seeds, keys, and installer media.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vmlite/
Default cache for downloaded cloud images and installer media.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show help:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite
vmlite help stop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a starter configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite init
vmlite init --template minimal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create or start a VM:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite up
vmlite up --connect qemu:///system vm.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop a managed VM by name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite stop dev
vmlite stop --force dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Finish an installer and run provisioners:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite provision vm.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate a configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vmlite validate vm.json
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime or configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
VM is not running, missing, or not created.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR virsh (1),
.BR virt\-install (1),
.BR qemu\-img (1)
